1. INTRODUCTION
==========================================================

The entertainment industry generates a vast amount of content every year. Finding relevant movies based on user interests has become a significant challenge. Recommendation systems help users discover movies that match their preferences and viewing habits.

This project focuses on developing a Content-Based Movie Recommendation System using Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques. The system recommends movies based on storyline similarity. Users can enter a movie storyline, and the application returns the top 5 most similar movies from the dataset.

The recommendation system is built using TF-IDF Vectorization and Cosine Similarity techniques. A user-friendly Streamlit application has been developed to provide an interactive interface for movie recommendations.

==========================================================
2. PROBLEM STATEMENT
==========================================================

The objective of this project is to build a movie recommendation system that recommends movies based on storyline similarity.

The system should:

• Extract movie information from IMDb.
• Store movie names and storylines in CSV format.
• Perform Natural Language Processing on movie storylines.
• Convert textual data into numerical feature vectors.
• Calculate similarity between movies.
• Recommend the top 5 most similar movies.
• Provide recommendations through a Streamlit web application.

==========================================================
3. BUSINESS USE CASES
==========================================================

Movie Recommendation:
Users can receive movie suggestions based on storyline similarity.

Personalized Entertainment:
The recommendation engine helps users discover movies that match their interests.

Content Discovery:
The system enables users to explore new movies with similar themes and plots.

