==========================================================
8. DATA COLLECTION AND SCRAPING
==========================================================

IMDb movie information was collected and stored in CSV format.

Tools Used:

• Selenium
• Python
• Pandas

Scraping Process:

1. Access IMDb movie pages.
2. Extract movie names.
3. Extract movie storylines.
4. Store data in CSV format.

Output File:

scraped_movies.csv

(INSERT selenium_scraper.png SCREENSHOT HERE)

==========================================================
9. DATA PREPROCESSING
==========================================================

Storyline text was cleaned and prepared before analysis.

Preprocessing Steps:

• Convert text to lowercase
• Remove punctuation
• Remove special characters
• Remove stopwords
• Tokenization
• Text normalization

Example:

Original Text:
A young wizard begins his journey at a magical school.

Processed Text:
young wizard begins journey magical school

==========================================================
10. FEATURE ENGINEERING
==========================================================

To perform recommendation analysis, textual storylines were transformed into numerical vectors.

Technique Used:

TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency)

Benefits:

• Captures important words
• Reduces influence of common words
• Creates numerical feature vectors

Library Used:

from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer

==========================================================
11. RECOMMENDATION ENGINE
==========================================================

The recommendation system uses Cosine Similarity.

Process:

1. Convert storylines into TF-IDF vectors.
2. Calculate similarity scores.
3. Rank movies by similarity.
4. Return top 5 recommendations.

Library Used:

from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity

Output:

Top 5 most similar movies are returned to the user.

